>> title: Chicken Feet
>> category: Stews & Braises
>> tags: chicken, chinese, black bean, deep-fry, steamed
>> counters: Dim Sum Counter
>> aka: fung zao, fung jao, 鳳爪, 豉汁蒸鳳爪, phoenix claws, braised chicken feet, chicken paws
>> servings: 4
>> time: 4 hr
>> slack: narrow — the feet have to be bone dry before they meet the oil, because water left on them spits and that is a burn
>> step.1: blanch 5 min, dry them right through
>> step.2: fry 350°F (175°C) 5 min, until the skin blisters
>> step.3: soak in ice water 1 hr, until they plump and wrinkle
>> step.4: simmer in the black bean sauce 1 hr
>> step.5: steam 30 min, until the sauce clings

Blanch @chicken feet{2%lb}(900 g; nails clipped off) in a #pot{} of boiling water with @Shaoxing wine{2%Tbs} and @fresh ginger{4%slices}(coin-sized) for ~blanch{5%min}, then drain them and dry them right through with a cloth.

Fry @&(~1)feet{} in @peanut oil{6%cups}(1.4 L; at 350°F/175°C) in a deep #pot{}, a handful at a time and with the lid to hand, for ~fry{5%min}, until the skin has gone gold and puffed away from the bone.

Soak @&(~1)fried feet{} in @iced water{8%cups}(1.9 L) for ~soak{1%hr}.

Simmer @&(~1)feet{} with @fermented black beans{2%Tbs}(rinsed and lightly mashed), @garlic{4%cloves}(minced), @oyster sauce{2%Tbs}, @light soy sauce{1%Tbs}, @Shaoxing wine{1%Tbs}, @sugar{1%Tbs}, @star anise{2%pods}, @dried red chiles{2} and @water{2%cups}(475 mL) in a #pot{} for ~simmer{1%hr}, until a bone pulls free without a fight.

Steam @&(~1)feet{} in their sauce in a #bowl{} set inside a #steamer{}, scattered with @scallions{2}(sliced), for ~steam{30%min}.
